    <span class="docs-eyebrow">Overview</span>
    <h1>What is the eLearning Design System?</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">A reusable system of learning principles, visual foundations, experience patterns, components, platform standards and governance for coherent digital learning experiences.</p>

    <div class="docs-module" id="purpose">
      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Create a coherent learner experience across platforms and course types.</li>
        <li>Reduce reinvention through documented patterns, components and shared production standards.</li>
        <li>Improve delivery speed, accessibility, maintainability and readiness for future brand change.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-module" id="audiences">
      <h2>Audiences</h2>
      <table class="docs-field-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Audience</th><th>What the system provides</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Executives &amp; sponsors</td><td>Strategic direction, scope, governance model and investment rationale.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Designers &amp; developers</td><td>Learning patterns, components, implementation standards, versioning and technical references.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Subject matter experts</td><td>A clearer explanation of how content is structured and why particular patterns are used.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Platform administrators</td><td>A consistent model for applying the system within Moodle, Rise and future tools.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-module" id="architecture">
      <h2>System architecture</h2>
      <table class="docs-field-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What it governs</th><th>What it does not contain</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Core system</td><td>Learning intent, foundation roles, patterns, component contracts and governance.</td><td>Organisation-specific branding or platform code.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Implementation</td><td>Theme values, technical namespace, platform behaviour and production assets.</td><td>Course-specific approved copy or scenarios.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Course application</td><td>Source-controlled content, sequence, scenarios, media and release evidence.</td><td>Unreviewed changes to the reusable system.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-module" id="implementations">
      <h2>Implementations</h2>
      <p>The core is deliberately neutral. Organisation and platform decisions live in named implementation layers so they can evolve without redefining the system. The <a href="{{ base }}implementations/index.html">implementation directory</a> records the available themes, platforms and current production evidence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-module" id="maturity">
      <h2>Maturity and roadmap</h2>
      <p>The system has moved from course-by-course discovery to formal consolidation. Its first implementation was proven through a substantial child-protection course family. This site represents Roadmap Phase 5 — Document and demonstrate — reached ahead of the completed audit and accessibility gate, so several entries are marked accordingly. See <a href="{{ base }}governance/index.html">Governance</a> for the full lifecycle model and current open decisions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-module" id="how-to-use">
      <h2>How to use this site</h2>
      <p>Executives and sponsors: read this Overview and Governance. Designers: start with Learning design and Learning patterns. Developers: use Components, then enter the relevant Implementation for production detail. Reviewers: use the accessibility fields on each component page and the checklists under Resources.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
